WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.886
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C one, Book four.

2
00:00:05.186 --> 00:00:08.851
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.151 --> 00:00:15.066
Unit twenty: Sustainable Business. Today you will set conditions for green growth with provided that.

4
00:00:15.366 --> 00:00:17.948
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.877
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.717 --> 00:00:24.078
Sustainability.

7
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:29.765
Sustainability means meeting present needs without harming future generations.

8
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:33.847
Sustainability is now part of the company's core strategy.

9
00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:37.752
Your turn. Say: Sustainability.

10
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.938
Sustainability.

11
00:00:42.683 --> 00:00:43.475
ESG.

12
00:00:44.483 --> 00:00:49.374
ESG means environmental, social and governance criteria used to judge companies.

13
00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:53.074
Investors screen firms using ESG scores.

14
00:00:53.683 --> 00:00:56.312
Your turn. Say: ESG.

15
00:00:59.167 --> 00:00:59.947
ESG.

16
00:01:00.683 --> 00:01:01.963
Carbon footprint.

17
00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:07.968
Carbon footprint means the total greenhouse gases caused by an activity or organisation.

18
00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:12.069
Switching to solar power halved the factory's carbon footprint.

19
00:01:12.683 --> 00:01:15.997
Your turn. Say: Carbon footprint.

20
00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:20.136
Carbon footprint.

21
00:01:20.883 --> 00:01:22.233
Circular economy.

22
00:01:23.217 --> 00:01:28.490
Circular economy means a system that reuses and recycles materials instead of discarding them.

23
00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:32.546
In a circular economy, old clothes become new fabric.

24
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.452
Your turn. Say: Circular economy.

25
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.998
Circular economy.

26
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:42.960
Stakeholder.

27
00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:48.179
Stakeholder means anyone affected by or interested in a company's actions.

28
00:01:48.783 --> 00:01:51.897
Local fishermen are key stakeholders in the port project.

29
00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:55.298
Your turn. Say: Stakeholder.

30
00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.297
Stakeholder.

31
00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:00.981
Reporting.

32
00:02:01.983 --> 00:02:05.260
Reporting means publishing information about performance.

33
00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:09.336
Sustainability reporting must be honest to be credible.

34
00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:12.835
Your turn. Say: Reporting.

35
00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:16.701
Reporting.

36
00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:18.138
Green.

37
00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.858
Green means environmentally friendly.

38
00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:25.727
Green packaging made from banana leaves attracted tourists.

39
00:02:26.317 --> 00:02:28.621
Your turn. Say: Green.

40
00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.119
Green.

41
00:02:32.883 --> 00:02:34.221
Long-term value.

42
00:02:35.217 --> 00:02:38.563
Long-term value means benefits that last over many years.

43
00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:43.088
Energy efficiency creates long-term value for shareholders.

44
00:02:43.683 --> 00:02:46.521
Your turn. Say: Long-term value.

45
00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:52.237
Long-term value.

46
00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:56.823
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:57.683 --> 00:03:05.247
Visal, a Siem Reap hotel installed solar panels and stopped using plastic bottles. Isn't that just expensive branding?

48
00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:14.923
Not necessarily. The panels pay for themselves within five years, provided that electricity prices stay roughly where they are.

49
00:03:16.017 --> 00:03:17.996
And the guests? Do they care?

50
00:03:19.083 --> 00:03:26.751
Many do. Eco-conscious tourists will pay a premium, provided that the claims are genuine and verifiable.

51
00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.117
What if the claims are exaggerated?

52
00:03:31.217 --> 00:03:41.276
That's greenwashing, and it backfires badly. Sustainability builds long-term value only provided that reporting is honest.

53
00:03:42.433 --> 00:03:44.177
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:45.017 --> 00:03:48.038
Grammar focus: Conditional with provided that.

55
00:03:48.338 --> 00:03:49.571
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:50.283 --> 00:03:53.676
Profits can grow, provided that costs are managed.

57
00:03:54.583 --> 00:03:57.396
Guests will pay more provided that the claims are genuine.

58
00:03:58.283 --> 00:04:02.140
The panels pay for themselves as long as prices stay stable.

59
00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:12.579
'Provided that' means 'only if' and stresses that the condition is essential. Like 'if', it takes a present tense for future meaning: provided that costs fall (not 'will fall').

60
00:04:13.317 --> 00:04:18.082
Be careful! Don't say: Provided that costs will fall, we grow.

61
00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:23.681
Say: Provided that costs fall, we will grow.

62
00:04:23.981 --> 00:04:25.993
Present tense after 'provided that'.

63
00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.313
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.229
Can Green Pay?.

65
00:04:31.529 --> 00:04:36.071
For decades, sustainability was viewed as a cost that reduced profits.

66
00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:47.228
Today, many firms argue that environmental responsibility can create long-term value, provided that it is built into the core business rather than added as decoration.

67
00:04:48.233 --> 00:04:54.935
Energy efficiency lowers operating costs, while circular-economy models turn waste into new revenue streams.

68
00:04:55.933 --> 00:05:03.622
Investors increasingly use ESG criteria, rewarding companies that manage environmental and social risks well.

69
00:05:04.633 --> 00:05:11.463
However, the benefits materialise only provided that reporting is transparent, since greenwashing quickly destroys credibility.

70
00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:16.603
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:20.425
We will invest, provided that the bank blank the loan.

72
00:05:20.725 --> 00:05:24.274
A, will approve. B, approves. C, approved.

73
00:05:27.833 --> 00:05:29.694
The answer is B: approves.

74
00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:35.322
Environmental, social and governance criteria are called blank.

75
00:05:35.622 --> 00:05:39.473
A, ESG. B, carbon footprint. C, reporting.

76
00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:44.580
The answer is A: ESG.

77
00:05:45.717 --> 00:05:49.899
A system that reuses materials instead of discarding them is a blank.

78
00:05:50.199 --> 00:05:55.037
A, green economy. B, carbon footprint. C, circular economy.

79
00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:01.494
The answer is C: circular economy.

80
00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:04.406
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:06:04.706 --> 00:06:12.307
A, Provided that it will rain, we cancel.. B, Provided that it rains, we will cancel.. C, Provided that it rained, we will cancel..

82
00:06:15.867 --> 00:06:19.468
The answer is B: Provided that it rains, we will cancel..

83
00:06:20.617 --> 00:06:24.404
According to the reading, the benefits of sustainability depend on…

84
00:06:24.704 --> 00:06:30.006
A, transparent reporting. B, high prices. C, avoiding investors.

85
00:06:33.567 --> 00:06:36.182
The answer is A: transparent reporting.

86
00:06:37.367 --> 00:06:40.588
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:44.309
Can sustainable business also be profitable?

88
00:07:01.117 --> 00:07:02.745
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:03.045 --> 00:07:40.558
Yes, sustainable business can be profitable, provided that sustainability is part of the core strategy rather than a marketing slogan. Reducing energy and waste lowers costs, while many customers and investors now prefer responsible companies. A Cambodian hotel using solar power can cut expenses and attract eco-conscious tourists. However, some green investments take years to pay back, so firms need patient capital. In the long run, I think sustainability and profit increasingly point in the same direction.

90
00:07:40.858 --> 00:07:42.602
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:43.517 --> 00:07:48.003
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and conditional with provided that.

92
00:07:48.303 --> 00:07:53.661
Today's value is sustainability. Choose ways of living that protect the planet for the future.

93
00:07:53.961 --> 00:07:56.892
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

94
00:07:57.192 --> 00:07:59.891
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

